# Cloudflare Pages response headers.

# The service worker must never be held by an edge cache. vite-plugin-pwa is
# configured with registerType: 'autoUpdate', which only works if the browser can
# actually see that sw.js changed — a cached one pins players to an old build,
# and the symptom is a leaderboard that has quietly stopped moving. This is the
# one header here whose absence is a bug rather than a missing hardening.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Hashed by Vite, so the content at a given name can never change.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Deliberately no Content-Security-Policy here. A correct connect-src has to name
# both the Supabase project and the Fly API, neither of which is known when this
# file is committed — and a wrong one does not degrade, it breaks magic-link
# login outright. The exact directives to add once those URLs are settled are in
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, as a post-deploy step done with the site in front of you.
